Key findings from the CORSIKA 8 research are presented, focusing on the underlying physics governing hadronic interactions, as well as the development of a new Monte Carlo detector simulator.  An analysis of the emulsion chamber has been conducted, and recent updates to the CORSIKA 8 simulation code are outlined.  Recent results, including observations of the air shower maximum and the depth of the shower start, are discussed, as are prospects for future research.  A comprehensive list of the most recent contributions from the CORSIKA 8 team is provided at the end of this document. 

